        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove note about Safari time picker for `datetime-local`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27762</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27762"/>
        <updated>2025-09-05T15:34:55.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/644927?u=790461985bc61a38ef27bed89be1fdec9ace7cbc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Safari 14.1 and newer displays a time picker for <code class="notranslate">datetime-local</code>.<br>
<code class="notranslate">datetime-local</code> was not working correctly in one of the Safari tech previews but was fixed before the final 14.1 release.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">See the Safari 14.1 release note (<a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes" rel="nofollow">https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes</a>)</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Added support for HTML date, time, and datetime-local input types in macOS, enabling date and time controls in forms.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">This is confirmed by the according issue (comment 27): <a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27" rel="nofollow">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27</a></p>
<p dir="auto">More confirmations:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>With screenshot: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="717735603" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5646" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646/hovercard?comment_id=715180664&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646#issuecomment-715180664">Fyrd/caniuse#5646 (comment)</a></li>
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="728444766" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5669" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669/hovercard" href="https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669">Fyrd/caniuse#5669</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">A jsfiddle to test yourself: <a href="https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/" rel="nofollow">https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/</a></p>
